      "writtenOn": "2026-07-14T23:42:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This class can stand on its own, but looks awkward because it doesn\u0027t have any methods. Depending on its intended usage, maybe it can have an is_valid() getter so callers can check if initialization succeeded or not. If that existed, then this CL can add more tests and check is_valid(). However, I indirectly asked about this on the next CL, and the latest update on that CL is saying the caller is expected to call GetVisualRunsForLine() and that CL handles initialization failure.\n\nSo if GetVisualRunsForLine() is going to be the only method in this class, then I guess it may be better to merge the two CLs so it can be tested in a meaningful way.\n\nAgain, if there was a CL chained to show usage from production callers, that could help shape what is the best way to implement this class.\n\nFor reference, the \"avoid initialization that can fail if you can\u0027t signal an error.\" part in https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html#Doing_Work_in_Constructors is what\u0027s on my mind here.",
